== Impact from stats ==

Paladins are a tanking support class with great defensive skills and powerful spells set to help you keep your group alive. As a paladin, you are expected to have a high amount of hit points and AC to perform your main role as a tank and a decent mana pool to cast your aggro spells (flash of light and stun). 

* '''Wisdom''':  Will increase your mana pool.
* '''Strength''':  Will increase your damage output (albeit slightly).
* '''Dexterity''': Will increase the likelihood of procs (Ghoulbane, Fiery Avenger, and Fiery Defender come to mind).
* '''Charisma''': Will decrease the critical resist rate of the [[Lull]] line of spells.

== Religion ==

Paladins must choose a religion, as their magic powers flow from their devotion to their chosen god. There is only one significant item for paladins that your deity will affect, and that is the [[Natures Defender]] (Tunare only).  Your religion will also impact where your human or half-elf character can start.  Selections include [[Karana]], [[Rodcet Nife]], [[Erollisi Marr]], [[Brell Serilis]], [[Mithaniel Marr]], [[Prexus]], [[Tunare]], and [[Quellious]].  Depending on your race you will be given a different number of these deities to choose from.

You may also want to view [[Deity Specific Items]].

